WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.270
Since the beginning of "Star Wars" fans have
grown to love and hate both the Jedi and the

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.026
Sith, but there is a much wider galaxy out
there of Force users.

00:00:09.026 --> 00:00:10.526
Here are some of the best.

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:15.639
Although the Jedi Order stresses maintaining
"balance in the Force," it traditionally favors

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:21.640
the light side, which promotes defense, passivity,
and peace over darker traits like fear, anger,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.660
and hatred.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.369
However, other Force-sensitive beings truly
are all about balance.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:31.200
One such being is Bendu, an ancient being
introduced in the "Star Wars Rebels" third

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.340
season episode "Steps Into Shadow."

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.000
A Force-sensitive entity who lives on the
planet of Atollon, Bendu claims to represent

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.070
the center of the Force, residing between
the light and dark sides.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.809
Refusing to take sides in any conflict, Bendu
has still accumulated vast knowledge of the

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:48.320
Force over many years.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.199
Although Bendu claims not to interfere in
the affairs of the Jedi or the Sith, he does

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:56.880
aid Force-sensitive beings, including Jedi
Knight Kanan Jarrus.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.180
After Kanan loses his sight in a battle, the
imbalance he feels awakens Bendu.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.000
Not only does Bendu teach Kanan to use his
other senses to compensate for his lost sight,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.700
but he also counsels Kanan on his fears about
losing his apprentice, Ezra Bridger, to the

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.700
dark side.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.060
Bendu continues providing counsel to both
Kanan and Ezra in later episodes.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:20.520
While he seems largely benevolent, he's also
fiercely neutral and even claims it may be

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.939
the will of the Force to destroy the Jedi.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:28.250
"Star Wars" often focuses on stories of good
versus evil, but Bendu reminds audiences that

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.442
there are always shades of grey in between.

00:01:30.964 --> 00:01:36.140
A shaman and the Clan Mother of the Nightsisters
of Dathomir, Mother Talzin occupies an unusual

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.440
place in the Force.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.500
At first, it seems she was affiliated with
Darth Sidious, who promises to trade dark

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.260
side secrets with her.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.909
Instead, Sidious abducts Talzin's son, Maul,
and trains him as a Sith Lord.

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:53.850
Talzin seeks revenge against the Sith, eventually
using her magicks to resurrect Maul and empower

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.369
his brother Savage Opress so they could battle
Sidious.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:01.909
These feats cause her to lose her physical
body, yet she survives as a spirit and continues

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:04.320
affecting events on the physical plane.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.160
Even after she's permanently destroyed, Maul
and the others she'd helped continue fighting

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.050
in the Clone Wars and beyond.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.891
Interestingly, Talzin claims to not have a
natural connection to the Force, although

00:02:13.891 --> 00:02:16.860
the Nightsisters derive their powers from
the dark side.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.360
Her abilities are based on Dathomir-style
dark magicks, allowing her to use a form of

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.980
Force lightning, see the future through a
crystal ball, and transform others.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.870
Most notably when she gives Maul a new pair
of mechanical legs.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.670
While she undoubtedly uses the dark side,
her vendetta against the Sith makes her a

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.620
very different player in "Star Wars" power
struggles.

00:02:36.079 --> 00:02:40.260
When it comes to choosing the most notable
Jedi, several candidates come to mind.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.860
Jedi Master Yoda trained Jedi Knights for
centuries.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.530
Obi-Wan Kenobi was one of the Jedi Order's
most accomplished knights.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.090
However, Luke Skywalker, the focus of the
original trilogy, stands out as the most significant

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.560
Jedi of his time.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.550
What's remarkable about Luke is that he often
walks alone on his journey toward becoming

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.560
a Jedi.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.030
Although he receives training from both Obi-Wan
Kenobi and Yoda and studies texts left by

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:06.810
Jedi Masters from previous eras, the Jedi
are largely extinct by the time Luke begins

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.770
his training, requiring him to learn in unconventional
ways.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:15.360
This no doubt influences his scrappiness,
determination, nobility, and power.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.959
The Republic's Jedi Order fell before Luke's
birth largely because of the Jedi's hubris,

00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:22.240
casting doubt on their teachings and morals.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.750
Luke also allows himself to be guided by the
Force itself rather than one teacher, which

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.700
allows him to become a very different type
of Jedi.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.500
Although he favors peace and serenity, he's
not afraid to tap into his darker emotions,

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.610
as we see in his more aggressive fighting
style in "The Mandalorian" Season 2's episode

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:42.629
"The Rescue" or in his fight against Darth
Vader in "Return of the Jedi."

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:47.489
At his best, he's one of the most balanced
Jedi Masters and can attain almost unbelievable

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:50.100
levels of power through his connection to
the Force.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.096
There's a reason why he's known as "The Chosen
One."

00:03:53.096 --> 00:03:58.330
Having been both Jedi Knight and Sith Lord,
Anakin Skywalker walks a path that, while

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.310
devastating, ultimately is drawn by the will
of the Force.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:05.769
His incredibly high midi-chlorian count gave
him incredible potential and helps him achieve

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:10.500
mighty Force powers, yet his early life as
a slave, coupled with the Jedi Order's inability

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.250
to understand him, made him very unstable.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.069
"You're a slave?"

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:18.128
"I'm a person, and my name is Anakin."

00:04:18.128 --> 00:04:22.960
Ultimately, Anakin's distrust of the Jedi,
desire for power, and fear of losing his loved

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.020
ones cause him to fall to the dark side and
become Darth Sidious' apprentice Darth Vader.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.789
A battle with Obi-Wan Kenobi leaves him stripped
of much of his power, yet even then he shows

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:36.870
he was still obeying the will of the Force
by destroying both the old Jedi Order and

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.639
eventually the Sith in "Return of the Jedi,"
two institutions that, in Vader's time, no

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:43.810
longer bring balance to the Force.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:47.830
In the process, he allows his son, Luke, to
bring about a new Jedi Order potentially better

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.520
suited for its time.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.360
As a Sith Lord, Darth Vader is utterly ruthless
and consumed with self-loathing.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.830
Although he's able to find redemption by killing
Darth Sidious and living on as Anakin Skywalker's

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:03.350
Force Ghost, his journey is filled with pain
and suffering, showing that the Force can

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.110
be quite violent in its attempts to bring
balance.

00:05:06.278 --> 00:05:10.880
The apprentice of Anakin Skywalker, Ahsoka
Tano has been many things over her lifetime.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.900
Initially, it looked like she would become
a member of the Jedi Order, training as a

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:18.620
padawan under Anakin and serving as a general
during the Clone Wars.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:23.110
However, Ahsoka becomes disillusioned by the
Jedi Order and leaves after being falsely

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.970
accused of committing crimes.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.400
She spends several years traveling incognito
before resurfacing as the agent "Fulcrum"

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.670
in "Star Wars Rebels" to aid the emerging
Rebel Alliance.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:37.470
Later still, she strikes out on her own again,
in adventures we'll see in the upcoming "Ahsoka"

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.910
Disney + series.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:43.229
Although people like the Mandalorian refer
to Ahsoka as a Jedi, Ahsoka has made it very

00:05:43.229 --> 00:05:47.039
clear that she does not associate herself
with the Jedi Order anymore.

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:52.240
Nevertheless, she continues to practice her
Jedi skills and wields two white lightsabers,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.169
signifying her affiliation with neither Jedi
nor Sith.

00:05:55.169 --> 00:05:59.030
While she continues to help those in need
and offer counsel to Jedi like Luke Skywalker,

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:04.220
at the end of the day, Ahsoka is one Force-sensitive
individual who defies classification.

00:06:04.638 --> 00:06:09.180
A member of Yoda's unnamed species, Grogu
is affiliated with many groups.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.240
Raised in the Jedi Temple before the events
of "The Mandalorian," Grogu had been trained

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.699
by many Jedi Masters and had tremendous Force
potential.

00:06:16.699 --> 00:06:21.840
However, his path to becoming a Jedi was cut
short when Order 66 caused clone troopers

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.870
to exterminate most of the Jedi.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.690
Hidden away by an unknown benefactor, Grogu
is eventually found and protected by Din Dijarin,

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:31.889
the Mandalorian, who comes to care for him
like a son.

00:06:31.889 --> 00:06:35.850
While the Mandalorian helps Grogu reunite
with the Jedi, the Child eventually decides

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.560
this path is not for him.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.890
Forced to choose between a life with the Mandalorian
or a life with the Jedi by Luke Skywalker,

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:46.330
Grogu chooses to reunite with Din Dijarin,
who looks like he'll train Grogu in the ways

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.220
of the Mandalorians in "The Mandalorian" Season
3.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.849
If Grogu does indeed decide to use his Force
abilities as a Mandalorian foundling, he won't

00:06:53.849 --> 00:06:54.979
be the first one.

00:06:54.979 --> 00:07:00.351
The legendary Tarre Vizsla was a Force-sensitive
Mandalorian who was inducted into the Jedi Order.

00:07:00.351 --> 00:07:05.060
He crafted the Darksaber, a weapon that came
to signify the rule of Mandalore.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:09.080
Although Luke claims Grogu could only live
as a Mandalorian or a Jedi, it's still very

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.350
possible Grogu can do both.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:15.870
Members of Yoda's species live centuries,
meaning the 50-year-old infant has many different

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.678
career paths in his future.

00:07:17.965 --> 00:07:22.039
The Inquisitors offer a way for the Sith Order
to work around the "Rule of Two" established

00:07:22.039 --> 00:07:23.139
by Darth Bane.

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:25.762
"Always two there are.

00:07:25.762 --> 00:07:28.589
No more, no less.

00:07:28.589 --> 00:07:32.460
A master and an apprentice."

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:35.970
Although the rule stipulates that there can
only be two Sith at one time, there are still

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:41.810
many dark side users in the galaxy, and Sith
Lords like Darth Sidious seek to exploit them.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:45.979
This leads to the creation of the Inquisitors,
Force-sensitive agents tasked by Palpatine

00:07:45.979 --> 00:07:50.240
with the job of hunting down any Jedi who
survived Order 66.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.490
Many of these Inquisitors are former Jedi
themselves, including a Pau'an Jedi Temple

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:58.690
guard who swore allegiance to the Dark Side
and became the Grand Inquisitor.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:03.230
As the leader of the other Inquisitors, the
Grand Inquisitor answers directly to Darth Vader.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:07.379
While he isn't a Sith Lord, the Grand Inquisitor
functions as a parallel to Darth Vader.

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:12.159
Much like Anakin Skywalker, the Grand Inquisitor
fell to the dark side after becoming resentful

00:08:12.159 --> 00:08:15.150
that the Jedi Order did not share its secrets
with him.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:20.430
He also regularly deceives and betrays his
fellow Inquisitors, including the Third Sister,

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:25.210
Reva, who sought to usurp his title in "Obi-Wan
Kenobi," showing that the worst dark side

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.900
users didn't have to be Sith.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:31.490
A member of the Guardian of the Whills, a
religious order that promotes unity with the

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.890
Force, the blind warrior monk Chirrut Îmwe
is a devout believer in the Force.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:39.981
Although he isn't a Jedi, Chirrut appears
to be Force-sensitive and can use the Force

00:08:39.981 --> 00:08:43.330
to perceive his surroundings and accomplish
miraculous feats.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:47.519
In "Rogue One: A Star Wars Story," he takes
out an entire gang of Stormtroopers using

00:08:47.519 --> 00:08:52.339
only a wooden stick, blows a ship out of the
sky with his lightbow, and walks through a

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:57.220
firefight without getting hit by a single
blaster shot, although he dies in a subsequent

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.300
explosion.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.330
Chirrut also feels the Force around certain
objects and beings.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:05.500
He can sense a kyber crystal — the power
source of a Jedi's lightsaber — around Jyn

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.500
Erso's neck.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:11.180
Later, he feels the Force moving "darkly"
around Cassian Andor, and correctly predicts

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.920
Cassian is preparing to assassinate someone.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.540
While his powers appear low-level compared
to the more exotic abilities of the Jedi and

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:22.200
the Sith, Chirrut's faith in the Force is
unshakeable, and he willingly submits himself

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.870
to its will, up to his death.

00:09:24.308 --> 00:09:29.230
As the daughter of Anakin Skywalker and the
sister of Luke Skywalker, Princess Leia Organa

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.890
possesses the potential to wield Force powers.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:36.220
Unlike her father and brother, however, Leia
chooses not to follow the path of the Jedi,

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.200
opting instead to lead freedom fighters as
a general.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:43.269
That's not to say that Leia hasn't manifested
Force abilities, or that she's incapable of

00:09:43.269 --> 00:09:45.399
tapping into her innate powers.

00:09:45.399 --> 00:09:49.910
Even as a child, Leia is able to resist an
Inquisitor mind probe in "Obi-Wan Kenobi,"

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:53.990
a feat she replicates as a young adult in
"Star Wars: Episode IV — A New Hope."

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.750
"Her resistance to the mind probe is considerable.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:00.731
It will be some time before we can extract
any information from her."

00:10:00.731 --> 00:10:04.800
She also has an instinctive connection to
her brother, Luke, and can sense his presence

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:08.380
in "The Empire Strikes Back" and guide the
Millennium Falcon back to him.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:12.209
In "The Rise of Skywalker," we learn that
Leia had been trained by Luke, but stopped

00:10:12.209 --> 00:10:15.180
after believing her son would die at the end
of her Jedi path.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.820
Nevertheless, Leia still uses her Jedi abilities
to survive in battle after being blown out

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.779
to space and later manifests as a Force Ghost
along with Luke.

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:28.380
Some may feel that someone with her degree
of Force potential should be a Jedi, yet Leia

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.529
invariably charts her own course.

00:10:31.092 --> 00:10:36.310
Older than even Jedi Master Yoda, Maz Kanata
is over a thousand years old by the beginning

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.750
of "The Force Awakens."

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.070
Although she tells Rey,

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.260
"I am no Jedi, but I know the Force."

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:45.620
Maz is Force-sensitive and has knowledge of
the Force.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.399
This enables her to chart her own path and
be a largely benevolent being who still has

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:53.010
no problem dealing with the scummier folk
in the "Star Wars" galaxy.

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:58.459
Indeed, Maz gains a reputation as a "pirate
queen," hosting traveling smugglers and criminals

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:03.820
at her castle, which resembles a somewhat
cleaner version of Tatooine's Mos Eisley Cantina.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:08.530
It's not surprising that she develops a friendship
with Han Solo or refers to his first mate,

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.210
Chewbacca, as her "boyfriend."

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.959
Nevertheless, Maz follows her own code, prohibiting
any of the criminals who sought sanctuary

00:11:14.959 --> 00:11:18.310
at her home from engaging in politics, war,
or fighting.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:22.339
Maz's role in the story lies in her talent
for collecting antiques and treasures from

00:11:22.339 --> 00:11:23.427
across the galaxy.

00:11:23.427 --> 00:11:27.650
Many of these items speak to her through the
Force, letting her know which relics she needs

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:32.960
to protect and safeguard, particularly Anakin
Skywalker's lightsaber, which was passed down

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.640
to Luke by Obi-Wan Kenobi, which she then
passes on to Rey.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:41.029
Maz's long lifespan and ability to safely
navigate through the criminal underworld make

00:11:41.029 --> 00:11:45.920
her the ideal guardian for Jedi relics and
other forgotten treasures, while her reverence

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.181
for the Force ensures these items go to the
right owners in time.

